⑩00000109⑿
易考范文十二
⑩00000339⑿
As is vividly depicted in the picture,
⑩00000776⑿
a man is exerting himself to grab money in the air,
⑩00001148⑿
a voluminous book in hand.
⑩00001389⑿
On the book are several big words—academic fraud.
⑩00001936⑿
Obviously the painter intends to condemn the intellectuals
⑩00002351⑿
who barter their honesty for fame or money.
⑩00002701⑿
Recently, mounting negative reports about some prestigious professors
⑩00003270⑿
have aroused public concern over intellectual integrity.
⑩00003686⑿
These professors, in spite of their high reputation,
⑩00004079⑿
are charged with plagiarizing others' research findings
⑩00004473⑿
or inventing scientific data.
⑩00004768⑿
A reliable survey of 180 researchers indicates that
⑩00005217⑿
approximately 60% of them confessed they paid to have papers
⑩00005709⑿
published in academic journals and that 40% of them said
⑩00010113⑿
they once copied others' work.
⑩00010332⑿
To make matters worse,
⑩00010518⑿
scholars lacking in professional integrity exert a bad influence on young students,
⑩00011098⑿
who followed the trend instead of pursuing innovation.
⑩00011459⑿
There is no doubt that this phenomenon has blocked the country's scientific development.
⑩00012115⑿
Therefore it is high time that
⑩00012444⑿
administration concerned took measures to curb the misconducts
⑩00012824⑿
and encourage creativity in academic field.
⑩00013185⑿
Of supreme importance is transparency,
⑩00013590⑿
which enables the government to oversee researchers’ work.
⑩00013995⑿
The eradication of academic dishonesty, I am convinced,
⑩00014399⑿
will clear the obstacles that prevent us from becoming a country of innovation and vitality.
